    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a3">

                <pb facs="0846" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    143.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Arias to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I have the honor to send for your
                    excellency’s information a copy of a communication from the war department, as
                    to the most recent steps taken to effect the arrest of Alexander D.
                    Hamilton.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, your excellency’s obedient servant,</p>
                <p>(Through illness of the minister.)</p>
                <closer><signed>JUAN D. ARIAS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief
                        Clerk.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
